 * Packing/unpacking _initial.pak\initial.cache_block_ (various game data: UI layout, settings, translations, etc.)
 
 ### SnowPakTool Desktop UI
+
+**Editors → Frame addons** lists frame attachments, roof racks and service equipment using the same read-only table, description and source-property view as Addons and Cargo. The main table shows cargo slots, fuel/water capacity, repair points, spare wheels, price, unlock rank, exploration lock, install socket, content and ID, with shared column sorting/filtering. Selecting a row shows all XML properties and source files below. Explicit file parents supply inherited summary values; templates remain visible without expansion, so blank capacities are unresolved rather than assumed zero. Install sockets do not establish complete truck compatibility. Reload reads the current workspace in the background; no game data is edited.
 
 A **slot-based upgrade randomizer** is available in **Randomizer → Upgrades**. Randomize upgrades builds the full component catalog from the workspace, resolves composite tire IDs, uses current obtainable map-truck previews plus direct garage/contract rewards, and saves a draft under `workspace/upgrade-randomization/draft.json`. Region progression must be finalized. Only owned regions are generated; replacement eligibility uses enabled trucks and explicit tire-pack ownership. Each pickup retains its original type, and metal detectors stay fixed. Truck-specific slots prefer unused local-compatible parts; shared slots use all eligible shared parts without a purchase-only restriction, with an extra foreign preference in the first region. Fallbacks broaden the same-type pool before reuse. Stock/default-only and objective-locked replacements are excluded conservatively. There is no locality quota. See [the planner and input contract](upgrade-distribution-draft.md).
 
